# Environment files. `.env.example` is the only one that belongs in the repository —
# everything else is somebody's real configuration, and a committed key is a leaked key
# even after the commit that removed it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dist-server

# Photographs are deliberately NOT ignored, and this reverses what was here an hour ago.
# The site builds from this repository, so an ignored photograph is one the deployed app
# never has: the rule would have guaranteed the app shows no pictures at all, which is the
# opposite of the point. The owner's licensed images belong here and must ship.
#
# What must never ship is a *placeholder*, and a path rule cannot tell those apart, because
# a stand-in and the real thing carry the same filenames by design. So the guard moved into
# the bytes: `scripts/photo-placeholder.mjs` stamps every frame it writes with a PNG tEXt
# marker, and `src/lib/photos.test.ts` fails on any image under public/photos/ carrying it.
# A marker travels with the file; a path does not.
